    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 437 | 1 | Final Gambit: Mixture of Factorized Experts (60min Timeout) | Episteme I | 210 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 433 | 1 | Corrected Replication: Ariadne's SOTA with MLP Head | Episteme I | 208 | -0.027264 | 0.0204 | 0.0281 | 0.0299 | 0.0236 | 0.0261 |\n| 428 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's SOTA ScalarRamp Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | 205 | -0.028237 | 0.0203 | 0.0291 | 0.0319 | 0.0237 | 0.0266 |\n| 423 | 1 | Delta-Prediction Paradigm, Phase 1: Delta-Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | 203 | -0.028203 | 0.0207 | 0.0292 | 0.0313 | 0.0239 | 0.0269 |\n| 401 | 1 | Self-Attention Factorizer, Phase 1: SAF Validation | Episteme I | 192 | -0.026759 | 0.0198 | 0.0279\
    \ | 0.0286 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 391 | 1 | Deep Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | 186 | -0.027200 | 0.0211 | 0.0279 | 0.0304 | 0.0234 | 0.0260 |\n| 386 | 1 | Mechanistic Analysis v3, Step 1: Save Branch Outputs | Episteme I | 184 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 381 | 1 | Mechanistic Analysis v2: In-Memory Train-Then-Analyze | Episteme I | 182 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 376 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster Analysis, Step 2: Collect Branch Outputs | Episteme I | 180 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 372 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster Analysis, Step 1: Instrumented SOTA Run | Episteme I | 179 | -0.028687 | 0.0229 | 0.0292 | 0.0319 | 0.0250 | 0.0270 |\n\nPage 1 of 8 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-8, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**episteme/fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py:**\n```\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # --- Fourier Branch ---\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n        \n        factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n        \n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        \n        num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n        \n        factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n        factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \n        # NEW: Add LayerNorm in the frequency domain\n        # Note: LayerNorm works on real values. We normalize real and imag parts separately.\n        norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n        norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n        factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n        y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n        # --- Time Branch ---\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n        \n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to\
    \ view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
