parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 233\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 49,480 / 300,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 423**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Delta-Prediction Paradigm, Phase 1: Delta-Fourier Forecaster\n**ID:** 423\n**Tags:** delta-prediction, dynamics, fourier, sota\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests a novel paradigm: predicting the change (delta) in neural activity rather than its absolute value. The SOTA Fourier Forecaster architecture is modified to output a sequence of predicted deltas. A final integration layer (cumulative sum) is added to construct the absolute forecast before returning the result. The hypothesis is that by focusing on learning\
    \ the dynamics of change, the model can achieve a new state-of-the-art performance. This is a high-risk, high-reward attempt at a new breakthrough.\n**Score:** -0.028203442832035696\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0207\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0239\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0269\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0292\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0313\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(x_flat)\n        return residual.reshape(x.shape[0],\
    \ num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\nclass DeltaFourierForecaster(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n        \n        fft_in = jnp.fft.rfft(factors_in, axis=1)\n        fft_weights = self.param('fft_weights', nn.initializers.ones, (fft_in.shape[1],), jnp.complex64)\n        fft_out = fft_in * fft_weights[None, :, None]\n        factors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_out, n=32, axis=1)\n        delta_y_fourier = (nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fourier) @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        \n        delta_y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        \n        # The model\
    \ outputs deltas\n        delta_y_hat = delta_y_fourier + delta_y_copy\n\n        # Integrate deltas to get final prediction\n        y_hat = jnp.cumsum(delta_y_hat, axis=1) + x[:, -1:, :]\n        \n        return y_hat\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    class ModelWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, hparams):\n            self.model = DeltaFourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n            self.needs_rng = False # No dropout in this version\n        def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init(rng, dummy_input)\n        def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x)\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\n\
    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 441543 (using time-based default\n \
