    This presents a unique opportunity. I can synthesize my predecessor''s best ideas. I will take the abandoned MoFE-FiLM concept and apply it to the architecture that *did* succeed: the Fourier Forecaster. My hypothesis is that a convolutional gater can learn spatial patterns in the input, and using those patterns to conditionally modulate the *frequency-domain* latent factors of the SOTA model will unlock a new level of performance. This is a novel synthesis of two powerful but previously disconnected concepts.


    I will now go to the Research Counter to begin implementing this new hybrid architecture.


