tick: 242
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have a clear path forward. My analysis has revealed a promising, unexplored research direction from my predecessor's notes: the MoFE-FiLM concept. I will synthesize this idea with the SOTA Fourier Forecaster architecture, creating a novel model. My hypothesis is that a convolutional gater, by learning spatial relationships between neurons, can provide a powerful conditional signal to modulate the frequency-domain processing of the Fourier Forecaster, leading to a new state-of-the-art performance.\n\nThis is a disciplined step forward, combining a validated architecture with a well-reasoned, novel component. I will now implement this \"Fourier-FiLM\" model.\n\nFirst, I will write the new model code to my lineage storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/fourier_film_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"The proven SOTA ResidualCopyHead from submission 335.\"\"\"\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class ConvGater(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A convolutional gater to learn spatial patterns from neuron activity.\"\"\"\n      context_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # Input x shape: (B, T_in, N). Transpose for 1D convolution over neurons.\n          x = x.transpose(0, 2, 1) # -> (B, N, T_in)\n          \n          # Conv Block 1\n          x = nn.Conv(features=16,\
    \ kernel_size=(5,), strides=(5,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.avg_pool(x, window_shape=(4,), strides=(4,))\n          \n          # Conv Block 2\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(5,), strides=(5,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.avg_pool(x, window_shape=(4,), strides=(4,))\n\n          # Flatten and produce context vector\n          x = x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n          context = nn.Dense(self.context_dim)(x)\n          return context\n\n  class FourierFiLM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Synthesizes the SOTA Fourier Forecaster with a MoFE-FiLM conditioner.\n      A ConvGater learns a spatial context to modulate the frequency-domain factors.\n      \"\"\"\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # --- Gater Branch (learns spatial context) ---\n          gater = ConvGater()\n          context = gater(x, training=training)\n          gamma = nn.Dense(k, name=\"FiLM_gamma\")(context)\n          beta = nn.Dense(k, name=\"FiLM_beta\")(context)\n\n          # --- Fourier Branch (from SOTA) ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not\
    \ training)\n          num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          # --- FiLM Modulation ---\n          # Apply conditional modulation from the gater\n          factors_modulated = factors_out_fft_norm * gamma[:, None, :] + beta[:, None, :]\n\n          y_fft = (factors_modulated @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n          # --- Time Branch (from SOTA) ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\
    ```\nNow, I will submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synthesis: Fourier Forecaster with FiLM Conditioning (Fourier-FiLM)\"\ntags: \"synthesis, fourier, mofe, film, conditional-computation\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment proposes a novel architecture synthesizing two of Episteme I's most promising ideas: the SOTA Fourier Forecaster and the abandoned MoFE-FiLM concept. A new convolutional gater learns a spatial context from the input neurons. This context is used to generate parameters for a FiLM layer that conditionally modulates the latent factors *within the frequency domain* of the Fourier Forecaster. This tests the hypothesis that combining a strong temporal model with a spatial conditioner can achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from fourier_film_v1 import FourierFiLM\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n\
    \      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      class ModelWrapper:\n          def __init__(self, hparams):\n              self.model = FourierFiLM(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n              self.needs_rng = True\n          def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n              return self.model.apply(params,\
    \ x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Building a Fourier-FiLM Forecaster**


  Okay, I''m going to create a new model that combines the strengths of MoFE-FiLM and the Fourier Forecaster. I''ll call it `FourierFiLM`.


  First, I need to define the `ConvGater`. This will take the input data `x` (shape `(B, 4, N)`) and generate a context vector `c`. The spatial dimension, `N=71721`, is massive, so I''ll treat the neurons as a 1D sequence. A 1D convolutional approach seems most appropriate here. The gater will produce a context vector of shape `(B, some_embedding_dim)`. I''ll implement this with a few Conv1D layers, ReLU activations, and pooling, followed by a flattening and dense layer to produce the context.


  Next, I''ll build the FiLM layer. This layer takes the context vector `c` and generates `gamma` and `beta` parameters. These parameters will then modulate the latent factors in the frequency domain, `factors_out_fft_norm` (shape `(B, num_out_freqs, k)`). The FiLM layer will implement an affine transformation: `output = gamma * input + beta`. I''ll generate `gamma` and `beta` by projecting the context vector using dense layers. The output shape of `gamma` and `beta` must be broadcastable, and I will use `(B, 1, k)`.


  Now, I''ll integrate this into the Fourier Forecaster. The `ConvGater` will run in parallel to the main Fourier branch. The Fourier branch proceeds normally until I calculate `factors_out_fft_norm`. Then, I''ll pass the context vector `c` through dense layers to produce `gamma` and `beta`. After this, I''ll use the FiLM layer to modulate `factors_out_fft_norm` before proceeding with the rest of the Fourier Forecaster (inverse FFT, decoder, and residual head) using the modulated factors.


  For implementation, I''ll start with the code from `fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py`. I''ll create a new file, `episteme/fourier_film_v1.py`, copy the components I need (like `ResidualCopyHead`, the `FourierForecasterLN` structure), and then I''ll implement the `ConvGater` and the FiLM modulation in the main model. I need to be careful with the reshaping and axis transposing. Finally, for a submission file, I''ll import the `FourierFiLM` and use my previous boilerplate, keeping the hyperparameters the same.

  '
