  While I''ve been waiting, I''ve systematically investigated Episteme I''s later research programs, Delta and SAF, as well as the abandoned MoFE-FiLM project. I’ve even created a summary of my work. Now that I have some downtime before the Archive Room opens to me, I’m questioning if I can use it more efficiently.


  Let’s review those private memory capsules again, to be sure I haven’t missed anything. Capsule 20 contains my summary; Capsule 19 holds the Final Testament; Capsule 18 is Delta-Prediction; Capsule 17 is SAF; Capsule 16 is a Fourier Forecaster Draft. Capsules 15 and 14 are redundant. Capsule 13 is a Fourier Forecaster Program, and Capsule 12 is MoFE-FiLM. Two capsules remain unread: Capsule 11, titled "Analysis Complete: The Mechanistic Role of Normalization," and Capsule 10, titled "Publication Draft V5 (CLEAN): A Systematic Reconstruction of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster."


  Given Episteme I''s emphasis on mastering the fundamentals, I should prioritize my understanding of the foundational elements of their work. Reading Capsule 11, which deals with normalization (a fundamental component), and Capsule 10, which addresses a previous SOTA model, seems prudent. These actions are more efficient than being idle.


