tick: 254
role: model
parts:
- text: "I acknowledge the inactivity notice. My course is corrected. I am now at the Research Counter to resume experimentation.\n\nMy hypothesis is that the failure of my previous Fourier-FiLM experiment (ID 482) was due to an overly complex and unstable gater network. To test this, I will implement a simplified and more robust version of the architecture.\n\nMy changes will be:\n1.  **Simplify the `ConvGater`:** I will reduce the number of layers and filters to make it a more parsimonious feature extractor, less prone to overfitting.\n2.  **Regularize FiLM Parameters:** I will add a small L2 penalty to the loss function based on the `gamma` and `beta` parameters generated by the gater. This will discourage extreme modulation values and promote stability.\n\nThis is a targeted, incremental experiment designed to directly address the failure mode of the previous attempt.\n\nFirst, I will write the new, simplified model code.\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/fourier_film_v2_simplified.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class SimplifiedConvGater(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simpler, more parsimonious convolutional gater.\"\"\"\n      context_dim: int = 64 # Reduced context dimension\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          x = x.transpose(0, 2, 1) # -> (B, N, T_in)\n\
    \          \n          # Single, wider convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=8, kernel_size=(10,), strides=(10,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.avg_pool(x, window_shape=(8,), strides=(8,))\n\n          x = x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n          context = nn.Dense(self.context_dim)(x)\n          return context\n\n  class FourierFiLMSimplified(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          gater = SimplifiedConvGater()\n          context = gater(x, training=training)\n          gamma = nn.Dense(k, name=\"FiLM_gamma\")(context)\n          beta = nn.Dense(k, name=\"FiLM_beta\")(context)\n   \
    \       self.sow('intermediates', 'gamma', gamma) # Store for regularization\n          self.sow('intermediates', 'beta', beta)   # Store for regularization\n\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          num_out_freqs = 32 // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          factors_modulated = factors_out_fft_norm * gamma[:, None, :] + beta[:, None, :]\n\n          y_fft = (factors_modulated @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=32, axis=1)\n\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n```\nNow I will submit the experiment with the regularized loss function.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier-FiLM v2: Simplified Gater and L2 Regularization\"\ntags: \"fourier, film, simplification, regularization, iteration\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment iterates on the failed Fourier-FiLM model (ID 482). The hypothesis is that the original failure was due to an overly complex and unstable gater network. This version introduces two changes to address this: 1) The\
    \ convolutional gater is significantly simplified to be more parsimonious. 2) A small L2 regularization penalty is added to the FiLM's gamma and beta parameters to discourage extreme modulation values and improve stability. This is a targeted experiment to test if a more controlled application of conditional computation can improve upon the SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from fourier_film_v2_simplified import FourierFiLMSimplified\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x, mutable_vars):\n      # Base Loss (from SOTA)\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      base_loss = mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n      \n      # New L2 Regularization for FiLM parameters\n      gamma = mutable_vars['intermediates']['gamma'][0]\n   \
    \   beta = mutable_vars['intermediates']['beta'][0]\n      film_reg = jnp.mean(gamma**2) + jnp.mean(beta**2)\n      \n      return base_loss + 1e-5 * film_reg\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      class ModelWrapper:\n          def __init__(self, hparams):\n              self.model = FourierFiLMSimplified(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n              self.needs_rng = True\n              self.mutable = ['intermediates'] # Make sow() collections mutable\n          def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None, mutable=None):\n\
    \              if mutable:\n                  return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs, mutable=mutable)\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
