- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 256\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 129,816 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 42 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fourier-FiLM v2: Simplified Gater and L2 Regularization' (ID: 495) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029243574535949324\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0203\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0240\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0306\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0321\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 495\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed signature mismatch in `compute_loss` function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe submission's `compute_loss` function\
    \ had an incorrect signature that didn't match the training system's expectations:\n\n**Original (incorrect):**\n```python\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x, mutable_vars):\n    # Tried to access mutable_vars['intermediates']['gamma'][0]\n    # and mutable_vars['intermediates']['beta'][0]\n```\n\n**Expected by system:**\n```python\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # Only 4 parameters, as defined in defaults.py:127\n```\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. The training system calls `compute_loss` with exactly 4 arguments (see `train_single.py:81`)\n2. The submission added a 5th parameter `mutable_vars` to access intermediate FiLM parameters\n3. During validation, `main.py:344` called the function with 4 args, causing: `TypeError: compute_loss() missing 1 required positional argument: 'mutable_vars'`\n\nThe agent was attempting to add L2 regularization on FiLM gamma/beta activations that were stored via `self.sow('intermediates', ...)` in the model.\
    \ However, these intermediate values are not passed to the loss function - they are only available inside the forward pass.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCorrected the `compute_loss` signature to match the system's requirements:\n\n1. **Removed `mutable_vars` parameter** - Changed signature from 5 to 4 parameters\n2. **Removed FiLM activation regularization** - The intermediate gamma/beta values from `sow()` are not accessible in the loss function\n3. **Kept the SOTA loss components** - Maintained MAE and curvature penalty (base_loss = mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen)\n\nThe fixed version in `submissions/submission_v2.py` now:\n- Has the correct 4-parameter signature\n- Uses only the SOTA loss (MAE + curvature penalty)\n- Successfully passes validation and runs without crashing\n\n## Technical Notes\nIf the agent wanted to regularize FiLM parameters, they would need to:\n- Extract the Dense layer weights from `params['params']['FiLM_gamma']` and `params['params']['FiLM_beta']`\n- Regularize the weights,\
    \ not the intermediate activations\n- However, the simple fix of removing this regularization is sufficient to make the code run\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the code runs successfully for 300+ seconds without errors, indicating the submission is now properly integrated with the training system.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom fourier_film_v2_simplified import FourierFiLMSimplified\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    \"\"\"Loss function with curvature penalty.\n\n    Note: Removed L2 regularization on FiLM intermediate values because\n    compute_loss only receives (predictions, targets, params, x) as per\n    the training system's signature. The intermediate\
    \ gamma/beta values\n    from sow() are not accessible here.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Base Loss (from SOTA)\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    base_loss = mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n    return base_loss\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    class ModelWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, hparams):\n            self.model = FourierFiLMSimplified(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n            self.needs_rng = True\n            self.mutable = ['intermediates'] # Make sow() collections mutable\n        def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n      \
    \      return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n        def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None, mutable=None):\n            if mutable:\n                return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs, mutable=mutable)\n            return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\n\
    Starting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 524877 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 524878\n\
    Hyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032241   |   0.029291  \n========================================\nTimeout after 4394.5s at epoch 1\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 4394.5s\nBest validation MAE: 0.029291\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.029291\nTraining time: 4426s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 524880\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU\
