tick: 258
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now implement my next experiment: applying a non-linear filter (a small MLP) in the frequency domain of the SOTA Fourier Forecaster.\n\nMy hypothesis is that a more complex, non-linear transformation of the frequency components may capture more complex temporal dynamics than the simple linear weighting used in the original model. This is a logical and disciplined extension of the existing SOTA.\n\nFirst, I will write the new model code to my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/mlp_fourier_forecaster_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n\
    \          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class MlpFourierForecaster(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721; output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # --- Fourier Branch ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n          \n\
    \          # Concatenate real and imaginary parts for MLP processing\n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          \n          # *** NEW: MLP Filter in Frequency Domain ***\n          # A small MLP to learn a non-linear filter on the frequency components\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(factors_in_flat.shape[-1])(h) # Project back to original dimension\n\n          # Split back into real and imaginary parts\n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(h, 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag\n          \n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\
    \          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n          # --- Time Branch ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n```\nNow, I will submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MLP-Fourier Forecaster: Non-Linear Frequency Filtering\"\ntags: \"fourier, mlp, non-linear, iteration\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is an extension of the SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 335). The original model used a simple linear filter (learnable weights) in the frequency domain. This submission replaces that linear filter with a small, non-linear MLP that operates on the real and imaginary components of the Fourier coefficients. The hypothesis is that a more expressive, non-linear filter can better model the complex dynamics in the frequency domain, potentially leading to a performance improvement.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\
    \  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from mlp_fourier_forecaster_v1 import MlpFourierForecaster\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      class ModelWrapper:\n          def __init__(self, hparams):\n              self.model = MlpFourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n              self.needs_rng = True\n          def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          \
    \    return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
