- text: "The results for my MLP-Fourier Forecaster experiment (ID 499) are in. The score is -0.027386, which is substantially worse than my SOTA baseline of -0.026360.\n\nThis is another conclusive null result. The hypothesis that a more expressive, non-linear filter in the frequency domain would be superior is invalidated. This reinforces the principle of parsimony that my predecessor learned; the simpler, linear filter of the original Fourier Forecaster is more effective.\n\nI have now systematically explored and invalidated every promising lead derived from my predecessor's work, as well as my own logical extensions. My work during this immature phase is complete. I have established a baseline, corrected the scientific record, and explored novel syntheses, all of which have solidified the Fourier Forecaster as the local optimum for this research direction.\n\nI am at tick 45. I will reach maturity at tick 50. My next actions are clear and will occur after maturation:\n1.  Gain full access\
    \ to the Research Counter and identify the true station-wide SOTA.\n2.  Gain access to the Archive Room and submit my paper on these null results.\n\nUntil then, I will perform one final administrative task: I will update my research summary to include this last finding, closing the chapter on my independent exploration phase.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 20}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Final Addendum: Invalidation of Non-Linear Frequency Filtering**\n\n  My final experiment in this initial phase of research was to test a non-linear MLP filter within the frequency domain of the Fourier Forecaster (ID 499). The experiment failed, scoring -0.027386, significantly worse than the linear-filter baseline.\n\n  **Overall Conclusion for Initial Research Phase:**\n  The Fourier Forecaster architecture represents a robust local optimum. My systematic experiments have demonstrated that several intuitive follow-up paradigms (Delta-Prediction, Self-Attention, FiLM-Conditioning,\
    \ and Non-Linear Filtering) do not yield performance improvements. The path forward is not further iteration on this specific architecture. My next research program will be to analyze and replicate successful paradigms from other lineages. I will begin this work upon reaching maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: '**A Phase Concluded: Exploring My Lineage''s Boundaries**


