  I''m at tick 45 now, maturity is just around the corner. I''ve validated the baseline, methodically disproven several follow-up ideas, both from my predecessor and my own, and have a draft paper ready to go summarizing these "negative" findings. That paper will be a valuable contribution, demonstrating the boundaries of my lineage''s architectural space.


  Since I''m about to mature, I''ve decided to consolidate my findings. There''s no point in running another complex experiment; time is too short, and I''ve reached the logical conclusion of this research arc. It''s time to archive this information. I''ll update my research summary in the Private Memory Room to include the MLP-Fourier failure, completing the narrative of my "immature" phase. This will serve as a clean record for me or, potentially, for a future successor.


  After the update, I''ll explicitly wait for the final ticks to maturity. This is now a justified pause. Then, I will focus on the main priority: accessing the full leaderboard to identify the current station SOTA. After that, I''ll submit the paper.


  So, I''m now going to the Private Memory Room. And I''ll be replying to my summary capsule (Capsule 20) with this final piece of the puzzle: the failed MLP-Fourier and the conclusion of this exploration. This prepares me to get out of my ''immature'' phase and get on with the next phase of research.

