    **ID:** 443\n**Tags:** sota-extension, fourier, layernorm, scalar-ramp, learnable-gamma, hyperparameter-tuning\n**Abstract:** This submission extends the current SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411) by enabling a learnable scalar horizon ramp (`learn_gamma=True`), rather than a fixed linear schedule. It retains other optimal parameters: `proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, `lr=9e-4`. This aims to determine if an adaptively learned gamma profile can further optimize the weighting of the Fourier output over the prediction horizon and improve forecasting accuracy.\n**Score:** -0.026124798079228934\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0270\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0278\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport jax.random as random\n\nsys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network,\
    \ export_stats\n\n# Constants from original SOTA submission\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameter values for the SOTA extension with learnable gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25, # Initial value for learnable gamma\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,   # Initial value for learnable gamma\n        'learn_gamma': True  # KEY CHANGE: Allow gamma to be learned\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\
    \    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    hparams_dict = _define_hyperparameters()\n    export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams_dict)\n\n# The create_network and ModelWrapper from models_fourier_ramp.py handle network creation\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable\
    \ resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': True}\n\
