parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 269\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Identify and understand the station's true SOTA.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 175,494 / 300,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Lumina I's SOTA Fourier-Ramp (ID 443)' (ID: 505) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02641591495708547\n\
    **Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0283\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 505\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dataclass field ordering error in SotaFourierRamp class. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `SotaFourierRamp` from `storage/episteme/sota_fourier_ramp.py`, which contained a Python dataclass field ordering violation:\n\n```python\nclass SotaFourierRamp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int              # no default\n    proj_rank: int           # no default\n    hidden_size: int         # no default\n    drop: float              # no default\n    output_horizon: int = 32 # HAS default value\n    learn_gamma: bool        # no default - ERROR!\n```\n\nIn Python dataclasses (and Flax nn.Module which uses dataclasses), **all fields without default values must\
    \ come before fields with default values**. The `learn_gamma` field violated this rule by appearing after `output_horizon` which has a default value of 32.\n\nThis caused a `TypeError` during module class initialization:\n```\nTypeError: non-default argument 'learn_gamma' follows default argument\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the complete fixed implementation:\n\n1. **Copied both classes** from `storage/episteme/sota_fourier_ramp.py`:\n   - `ResidualCopyHead` (no changes needed)\n   - `SotaFourierRamp` (fixed field ordering)\n\n2. **Reordered fields** in `SotaFourierRamp`:\n   ```python\n   class SotaFourierRamp(nn.Module):\n       rank_k: int\n       proj_rank: int\n       hidden_size: int\n       drop: float\n       learn_gamma: bool        # FIXED: Moved before output_horizon\n       output_horizon: int = 32\n   ```\n\n3. **Removed import** of the buggy module and included the fixed classes directly in submission_v2.py\n\n4. **Preserved all other\
    \ code** - The rest of the submission (hyperparameters, loss function, optimizer, ModelWrapper) remained unchanged as they were correct.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0, indicating the code is running without crashes. The training process is now executing properly with the Fourier-Ramp model architecture.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Error Type**: Python dataclass field ordering violation\n- **Affected Module**: `SotaFourierRamp` class in lineage storage\n- **Fix Strategy**: Inline the corrected class definitions to avoid dependency on buggy lineage file\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Result**: Code executes successfully, training in progress\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\
    \n# Fixed SotaFourierRamp class with correct field ordering\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass SotaFourierRamp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    hidden_size: int\n    drop: float\n    learn_gamma: bool  # FIXED: Moved before output_horizon to fix dataclass ordering\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        U\
    \ = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        F_out = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\
    \n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            # Initialize gamma_raw near sigmoid's linear region for stability\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1), (self.output_horizon,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        else: # Fixed linear ramp, not used by SOTA but kept for completeness\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, self.output_horizon, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = 0.25 + (0.99 - 0.25) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n\
    \        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'learn_gamma': True\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = SotaFourierRamp(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'],\n            drop=hparams['drop'],\n            learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params':\
    \ rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster\
    \ initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 546120 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 546123\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma':\
    \ True}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032831   |   0.029456  \n   2    |   0.029221   |   0.029436  \n   3    |   0.028995   |   0.029243  \n   4    |   0.028891   |   0.029193  \n   5    |   0.028849   |   0.029175  \n   6    |   0.028809   |   0.029142  \n   7    |   0.028773   |   0.029089  \n   8    |   0.028660   |   0.028960  \n   9    |   0.028456   |   0.028673  \n  10    |   0.028247   |   0.028484  \n  11    |   0.027986   |   0.028363  \n  12    |   0.027833   |   0.028119  \n  13    |   0.027675   |   0.028395  \n  14    |   0.027581   |   0.028111  \n  15    |   0.027488   |   0.027819  \n  16    |   0.027326   |   0.027708  \n  17    |   0.027127   |   0.027147  \n  18    |  \
    \ 0.026913   |   0.027320  \n  19    |   0.026745   |   0.027223  \n  20    |   0.026581   |   0.027023  \n  21    |   0.026470   |   0.027053  \n  22    |   0.026372   |   0.027208  \n  23    |   0.026272   |   0.026853  \n  24    |   0.026202   |   0.027067  \n  25    |   0.026082   |   0.027295  \n  26    |   0.026059   |   0.027063  \n  27    |   0.025937   |   0.026677  \n  28    |   0.025842   |   0.026681  \n  29    |   0.025823   |   0.026663  \n  30    |   0.025705   |   0.026840  \n  31    |   0.025665   |   0.026630  \n  32    |   0.025570   |   0.026805  \n  33    |   0.025509   |   0.026584  \n  34    |   0.025454   |   0.026853  \n  35    |   0.025396   |   0.026576  \n  36    |   0.025334   |   0.026478  \n  37    |   0.025274   |   0.026528  \n  38    |   0.025241   |   0.026430  \n  39    |   0.025187   |   0.026399  \n  40    |   0.025114   |   0.026653  \n  41    |   0.025059   |   0.026456  \n  42    |   0.025008   |   0.026617  \n  43    |   0.024992   |   0.026443\
