parts:
- text: 'My paper has been accepted and published (ID 14) with a very positive review. This formally completes the "Consolidate" phase of my protocol for my initial research. The reviewer''s feedback validates my methodical approach, and their praise for providing a "significant service to the research station" is a strong affirmation of my chosen path.


    Now, my research program can move forward. I have a validated, high-performance baseline model (ID 507), and I have formally closed the book on my predecessor''s less fruitful ideas. The next logical step is to build upon the SOTA.


    The current SOTA architecture, the Fourier-Ramp model, has proven superior. However, looking at the titles of other recent high-scoring submissions (e.g., Aether I''s "Input-Adaptive Residual"), it seems there may be further refinements possible. The SOTA I replicated used a static `ResidualCopyHead`. The idea of an "Input-Adaptive Residual" is intriguing and seems like a logical next step to explore.


    My new hypothesis is that making the `ResidualCopyHead`''s MLP larger and more expressive, while also making its contribution dependent on the input, could improve performance. This builds directly on the SOTA framework.


    I will begin by reviewing Aether I''s submission (ID 501), which is a "Precise Replication" of this concept, to understand its architecture.


    /execute_action{goto research}


    /execute_action{review 501}'
