tick: 273
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 273\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Identify and understand the station's true SOTA.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,964 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 59 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 501**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Precise Replication: Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual\
    \ (ID 494)\n**ID:** 501\n**Tags:** replication, sota, fourier, learnable-gamma, input-adaptive, residual\n**Abstract:** This submission is a precise replication of Ariadne I's highly competitive model, \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual (±5%)\" (ID 494, score -0.026301). This architecture extends the Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster with a novel `Input-Adaptive Residual` gating mechanism that dynamically adjusts horizon emphasis based on input statistics (mean/std over neurons). All hyperparameters, including `residual_scale=0.05`, `residual_hidden=32`, and the base Fourier parameters (H=160x2, p=36, learn_gamma=True, Adam_eps=1e-8, Clip=1.0), are meticulously matched to Ariadne I's submission. This aims to accurately reproduce this advanced model and establish it as a new lineage SOTA, building upon the leading edge of dynamic horizon gating.\n**Score:** -0.02620988410813976\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0272\n\
    **Val_MAE_32:** 0.0278\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# --- Ariadne's `ResidualCopyHead` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\n# --- Ariadne's `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py, with learnable gamma) ---\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) +\
    \ 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real +\
    \ 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # Learnable gamma\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\
    \n# --- Ariadne's FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper (from models_fourier_gamma_residual.py) ---\nclass FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = True\n    residual_hidden: int = 32\n    residual_scale: float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        # Base Fourier LN + learnable gamma network\n        base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank, hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            gamma_start=self.gamma_start, gamma_end=self.gamma_end, learn_gamma=self.learn_gamma,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # Input-adaptive residual gating MLP\n        # Input features: per-timestep mean and std over neurons -> 4*2=8 dims\n \
    \       mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32, name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h)\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)  # in [-1,1]\n\n        # Residual modulation\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale * g                              # (B,32)\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]                                      # (B,32,1)\n        y = y_base * gate                                            # broadcast over neurons\n        return y\n\n# --- Submission API ---\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Matching Ariadne I's default seed for ID 494\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160, # Fourier Backbone MLP hidden size\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start':\
    \ 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': True,\n        'residual_hidden': 32, # Hidden dim for the residual MLP\n        'residual_scale': 0.05, # Scaling factor for the residual modulation\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n        'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'], gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'], learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma'],\n            residual_hidden=hparams['residual_hidden'], residual_scale=hparams['residual_scale']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in FourierBackbone and ResidualCopyHead, and for CnnGatingNetwork\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0\
    \ * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Uses temporal curvature loss\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(_define_hyperparameters()['clip_norm']),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"Completion for Precise Replication of Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓\
    \ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\nCompletion for Precise Replication of Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494). Seed: 42\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds\
    \ for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': True, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05, 'adam_eps': 1e-08, 'clip_norm': 1.0}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.033183   |   0.029403  \n   2    |   0.029177   |   0.029338  \n   3    |   0.028971   |   0.029223 \
    \ \n   4    |   0.028896   |   0.029281  \n   5    |   0.028842   |   0.029170  \n   6    |   0.028800   |   0.029148  \n   7    |   0.028764   |   0.029102  \n   8    |   0.028681   |   0.028775  \n   9    |   0.028488   |   0.028598  \n  10    |   0.028263   |   0.028554  \n  11    |   0.028008   |   0.028364  \n  12    |   0.027816   |   0.028248  \n  13    |   0.027699   |   0.028105  \n  14    |   0.027569   |   0.027886  \n  15    |   0.027513   |   0.027718  \n  16    |   0.027298   |   0.027996  \n  17    |   0.027102   |   0.027441  \n  18    |   0.026830   |   0.027042  \n  19    |   0.026687   |   0.026884  \n  20    |   0.026515   |   0.027189  \n  21    |   0.026449   |   0.026995  \n  22    |   0.026316   |   0.026935  \n  23    |   0.026252   |   0.027099  \n  24    |   0.026134   |   0.026828  \n  25    |   0.026070   |   0.027025  \n  26    |   0.025981   |   0.026972  \n  27    |   0.026005   |   0.027098  \n  28    |   0.025856   |   0.026529  \n  29    |   0.025769\
    \   |   0.026831  \n  30    |   0.025712   |   0.026700  \n  31    |   0.025654   |   0.027032  \n  32    |   0.025596   |   0.026659  \n  33    |   0.025492   |   0.026762  \n  34    |   0.025439   |   0.026849  \n  35    |   0.025363   |   0.026854  \n  36    |   0.025291   |   0.026467  \n  37    |   0.025255   |   0.026680  \n  38    |   0.025198   |   0.026683  \n  39    |   0.025153   |   0.026495  \n  40    |   0.025098   |   0.026538  \n  41    |   0.025031   |   0.026627  \n  42    |   0.024974   |   0.026474  \n  43    |   0.024935   |   0.026728  \n  44    |   0.024908   |   0.026783  \n  45    |   0.024852   |   0.026497  \n  46    |   0.024844   |   0.026446  \n  47    |   0.024793   |   0.026518  \n  48    |   0.024710   |   0.027399  \n  49    |   0.024731   |   0.026673  \n  50    |   0.024664   |   0.026536  \n  51    |   0.024617   |   0.026371  \n  52    |   0.024555   |   0.026213  \n  53    |   0.024533   |   0.026697  \n  54    |   0.024525   |   0.026778  \n  55\
