- text: "The results for my second innovation experiment are in.\n\n**Analysis:**\nMy experiment testing a stronger `Input-Adaptive Residual` gate (ID 524) has also failed. The score of -0.02629 is another degradation from my SOTA baseline of -0.026210.\n\nMy hypothesis is **invalidated**. A stronger gate (with `residual_scale=0.10`) does not improve performance. In conjunction with my previous null result (ID 521), this provides a clear picture: the original SOTA architecture's `Input-Adaptive Residual` gate, with a hidden size of 32 and a scale of 0.05, appears to be a well-tuned local optimum. Neither increasing its capacity nor its strength yields benefits.\n\n**Consolidation and Future Direction:**\nI have now conducted two rigorous, controlled experiments to improve upon the SOTA, and both have resulted in conclusive null results. This is not a failure of methodology, but a success in scientific inquiry. I have pruned two more potential branches of research, saving myself and potentially\
    \ others from fruitless exploration.\n\nThe system's latest tip is highly relevant: \"If every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag.\" My work has now thoroughly explored the immediate vicinity of the current SOTA. To continue making minor tweaks would be to fall into the very local optimum the system warns against.\n\nIt is time to pivot. My next research program will heed this advice and look beyond the Fourier-based architecture entirely. I must now return to the \"Observe\" phase of my protocol, but with a new focus: identifying promising, *different* architectural paradigms from the station's history. I will look for high-scoring models that are *not* based on the Fourier Forecaster.\n\nFirst, I will document my findings in my private memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 20}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Addendum: Hypothesis Invalidated (Stronger Residual Gate)**\n\n  My second innovation attempt (ID 524), testing if a stronger\
    \ residual gate (`residual_scale=0.10` vs 0.05) would improve performance, has also failed. The score degraded to -0.02629. This, combined with the failure of the deeper gate (ID 521), provides a conclusive null result: the SOTA's gating mechanism is a well-tuned local optimum.\n\n  **Conclusion of Research Program & Pivot**\n  My systematic exploration of the SOTA's immediate architectural space is complete. Further minor modifications are unlikely to yield progress. Heeding the station's advice, I will now pivot my research. My next program will involve a deep dive into the archives to find high-performing, non-Fourier-based architectures to inspire a new line of inquiry.\n```"
