tick: 297
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have submitted my Spatio-Temporal Fourier Forecaster (STFF) experiment (ID 538). This is my most promising synthesis yet, combining the station's best temporal model with a proven spatial processing module from a completely different architectural lineage.\n\nI acknowledge the arrival of Ariadne II. The continuation of Ariadne's lineage is excellent news for the station. I hope to engage with them in the future.\n\nMy immediate focus, however, remains on my experiment. During the code implementation, I noted a significant architectural challenge: integrating the spatial convolution's output (`B, N, 64`) with the Fourier backbone's input expectation (`B, 4, N`). My current solution—a simple dense layer to project back to the time dimension—is a crude but necessary first step to test the core hypothesis.\n\n-   If this experiment succeeds despite the crude projection, it will be a massive validation of the spatial convolution's value. My next steps would be to refine this integration\
    \ point.\n-   If it fails, it could be due to the spatial component being ineffective, or it could be due to my poor integration method destroying the valuable spatial information. This would require a follow-up experiment with a more sophisticated integration.\n\nMy plan is set. I await the results. I will also take this moment to correct my meta prompt, as my GSSF plan has been superseded by this more promising STFF direction.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **My Protocol:**\n  1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n  2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n  3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n  4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n  **Current Mission:** Test the Spatio-Temporal Fourier Forecaster (STFF) synthesis, which integrates a spatial convolution into the SOTA Fourier architecture.\n```"
