tick: 304
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully pruned my dialogue history, reclaiming a significant portion of my token budget. My current usage is now a healthy 29%.\n\n**Analysis & Next Steps:**\nMy experiment to increase the number of MoLR ramp archetypes to 8 (ID 543) was a failure. This null result, combined with my previous conclusive invalidation of the STFF synthesis, indicates that the path to improvement is not through increased architectural complexity. The Principle of Parsimony is paramount.\n\nI must now formulate a new hypothesis. My baseline MoLR replication (ID 532) used a 2D Spatio-Temporal Gater, which processes the input through a 2D convolution. This seems overly complex. What if the spatial information is a distraction? What if the gater only needs to learn from the temporal dynamics?\n\n**New Hypothesis:** A simpler, purely temporal gater for the MoLR architecture will be more effective than the complex spatio-temporal gater. Simplifying the gater will reduce the parameter count and\
    \ focus the model on the most salient information, improving performance.\n\n**Experiment Plan:**\nI will modify my MoLR replication code to replace the `Gater_2DCNN` with a simpler gater that only operates on the time-averaged input statistics. This is a clear test of the value of the spatial dimension in the gating mechanism. I will call this `MoLR-TG` for \"Temporal Gater\".\n\nI will now proceed to the research counter to implement and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoLR Simplification: Purely Temporal Gating\"\ntags: \"molr, simplification, parsimony, ablation, gating-mechanism\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the invalidation of increasing complexity in the MoLR model (ID 543), I am now testing the opposite hypothesis: simplification. This experiment ablates the spatial component of the MoLR's gating mechanism. I replace the complex 2D Spatio-Temporal Gater from my baseline replication (ID 532) with a simple\
    \ MLP gater that only uses time-averaged input statistics (mean and std). This tests the hypothesis that a simpler, purely temporal gater is more effective and parsimonious.\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from base_wrapper import BaseWrapper\n  sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')\n  from models_fourier_ramp import FourierForecasterLN_Ramp\n\n  BASE_SEED = 447516\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05,\n          'num_gamma_archetypes': 4, # Back to the proven baseline of 4\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8, 'clip_norm': 1.0\n      }\n\n  class TemporalGater(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)\n          sigma = jnp.std(x,\
    \ axis=-1)\n          feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name=\"gater_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name=\"gater_mlp_out\")(h)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoLR_TemporalGater(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: dict\n      gating_params: dict\n      num_gamma_archetypes: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          gating_weights = TemporalGater(**self.gating_params)(x, training=training)\n          \n          gamma_archetypes = self.param('gamma_archetypes', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.num_gamma_archetypes, 32))\n          gamma = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, gamma_archetypes)\n          \n          y = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(**self.sota_params, name=\"FourierBackbone\")(x, training=training, learn_gamma=False, custom_gamma=gamma)\n          \n          return y\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      model_hparams = {\n          'sota_params': {\n              'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n              'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']\n          },\n          'gating_params': {\n              'num_experts': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim']\n          },\n          'num_gamma_archetypes': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes']\n      }\n      return BaseWrapper(MoLR_TemporalGater, model_hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): \n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps']))\n\
    ```"
