tick: 306
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 306\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Test the MoLR simplification hypothesis by replacing the spatio-temporal gater with a purely temporal one.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 90,038 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 92 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoLR Simplification: Purely Temporal Gating' (ID: 546) succeeded after\
    \ automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02661510134397216\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0283\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 546\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed API incompatibility error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to call `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp.__call__()` with keyword arguments `learn_gamma` and `custom_gamma`, but this model's `__call__` method only accepts `x` and `training` parameters.\n\nThe agent's architectural goal was to use a temporal gating mechanism to dynamically generate gamma values (temporal modulation weights) and pass them to the Fourier forecaster model. However, the imported `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` from `storage/lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py` doesn't support custom gamma injection at call time.\n\nAdditionally,\
    \ there was a minor path issue: the import used `storage/Lumina` (uppercase) when the actual directory is `storage/lumina` (lowercase).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Fixed Import Path**: Changed `sys.path.append('storage/Lumina')` to `sys.path.append('storage/lumina')` (lowercase)\n\n2. **Created Custom Wrapper Class**: Implemented `FourierWithCustomGamma` - a modified version of `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` that:\n   - Accepts an optional `custom_gamma` parameter in its `__call__` method\n   - Uses the provided custom gamma when available, falls back to default ramp behavior otherwise\n   - Includes an inline implementation of the residual copy head to avoid external dependencies\n\n3. **Updated MoLR_TemporalGater**: Modified to use `FourierWithCustomGamma` instead of the original `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp`, enabling the temporal gating mechanism to work as intended\n\nThe architecture now functions correctly:\n- `TemporalGater` analyzes\
    \ input statistics (mean/std) and produces gating weights\n- Gating weights combine with learned gamma archetypes to produce custom temporal modulation\n- `FourierWithCustomGamma` applies these custom modulations to its Fourier forecasts\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success with exit code 0, showing the code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing. This indicates the submission is now executing correctly through the full validation pipeline.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom base_wrapper import BaseWrapper\nsys.path.append('storage/lumina')  # Fixed: lowercase 'lumina' not 'Lumina'\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import FourierForecasterLN_Ramp\n\nBASE_SEED = 447516\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'num_gamma_archetypes': 4, # Back to the proven baseline of 4\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8, 'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass TemporalGater(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim, name=\"gater_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts, name=\"gater_mlp_out\")(h)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n# Custom wrapper for FourierForecasterLN_Ramp that supports custom gamma\nclass FourierWithCustomGamma(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    hidden_size: int\n    drop: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start:\
    \ float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False, custom_gamma=None):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n        # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B,\
    \ -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )                                                         \
    \        # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Use custom gamma if provided, otherwise use default ramp\n        if custom_gamma is not None:\n            gamma = custom_gamma[:, :, None]  # (B, 32, 1)\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]  # (1, 32, 1)\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head - inline implementation to avoid external dependency\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n     \
    \   residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n        y_copy = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        y_copy = y_copy.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                 # copy last 4 steps\n        y_copy = y_copy + residual\n\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\nclass MoLR_TemporalGater(nn.Module):\n    sota_params: dict\n    gating_params: dict\n    num_gamma_archetypes: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        gating_weights = TemporalGater(**self.gating_params)(x, training=training)\n\n        gamma_archetypes = self.param('gamma_archetypes', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.num_gamma_archetypes, 32))\n        gamma = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, gamma_archetypes)\n\n        # Use custom Fourier model that accepts custom_gamma\n        y = FourierWithCustomGamma(**self.sota_params, name=\"FourierBackbone\")(x, training=training, custom_gamma=gamma)\n\n        return y\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    model_hparams\
    \ = {\n        'sota_params': {\n            'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n            'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']\n        },\n        'gating_params': {\n            'num_experts': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim']\n        },\n        'num_gamma_archetypes': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes']\n    }\n    return BaseWrapper(MoLR_TemporalGater, model_hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps']))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\n\
    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 447516 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE:\
