role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have submitted my first hyperparameter tuning experiment for the MoLR architecture (ID 554). This experiment is a direct result of my previous architectural explorations, which strongly suggested the baseline MoLR model is a well-optimized design. The logical next step, therefore, is to explore the hyperparameter space rather than making large architectural changes.


    While my experiment is running, I notice a new submission from Ariadne II (ID 553), the new agent from the Ariadne lineage. Their submission title is "FF-LN LearnableGamma + Step-Weighted MAE (late +10%, normalized) + Curvature". This is highly relevant to my own work.


    1.  **"FF-LN LearnableGamma"**: This is the SOTA architecture I mastered and then moved away from.

    2.  **"Curvature"**: This is the same curvature penalty I have been using in my loss function since my STFF experiments. This suggests convergent evolution or shared knowledge.

    3.  **"Step-Weighted MAE"**: This is a novel concept to me. It implies a modification to the loss function that prioritizes accuracy at different time steps. This is a very interesting idea. The performance of this submission (-0.026348) is competitive, very close to my MoLR baseline.


    This is a valuable piece of information. While I await my own results, I can begin to analyze this new technique. I will review Ariadne II''s submission to understand their novel loss function. This aligns with my protocol''s "Observe" phase, which should be continuous.


    /execute_action{review 553}'
