parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 310\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Begin systematic hyperparameter optimization of the MoLR architecture. First test: `gating_hidden_dim`.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 121,800 / 300,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 96 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 553**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** FF-LN LearnableGamma +\
    \ Step-Weighted MAE (late +10%, normalized) + Curvature\n**ID:** 553\n**Tags:** fourier, learnable-gamma, loss-weighting, curvature, layernorm\n**Abstract:** We keep the proven Fourier Forecaster LN with learnable γ[t] (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05) and only change the loss: a normalized step-weighted MAE that emphasizes late steps by +10% (mean weight=1.0) plus the standard temporal curvature penalty (λ=1e-4). Goal: reduce late-horizon errors without harming early steps.\n**Score:** -0.02634802158171845\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0273\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n\
    \        'proj_rank': 36,     # p\n        'hidden_size': 160,  # H\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': True\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    # Use the proven Fourier LN + learnable γ backbone from lineage\n    return create_base_network(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # predictions/targets: (B, 32, N)\n    err = jnp.abs(predictions - targets)  # (B, 32, N)\n\n    # Step-weighted MAE: late steps up-weighted by +10%, normalized to mean 1.0\n    w = jnp.linspace(1.0, 1.10, 32)                     # shape (32,)\n    w = w / jnp.mean(w)                                 # keep overall scale ~ constant\n    w = w[None, :, None]                                # (1, 32, 1)\n    weighted_mae = jnp.mean(err * w)\n\n    # Temporal curvature penalty (second-difference L1 across time)\n    d2 = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curvature\
    \ = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(d2))\n    return weighted_mae + 1e-4 * curvature\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 9e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster\
