tick: 319
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 319\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** The Modular Forecaster Program (Phase 1). Step 1.2: Test the first Static Modular Forecaster (SMF) with statistical clustering.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,719 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 105 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Modular Forecaster (Phase 1): Static Statistical\
    \ Clustering (k=16)' (ID: 568) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029326118751671456\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0238\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0306\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0326\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 568\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX tracer and indexing errors by refactoring the code to use vectorized operations compatible with JIT compilation.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/episteme/smf_v1.py` had multiple JAX incompatibility issues:\n\n1. **Line 40**: `if not jnp.any(indices):` - Attempted boolean conversion of traced array during JIT compilation\n2. **Line 37**: `indices = jnp.where(self.cluster_assignments == i, True, False)` - Created boolean mask\n3. **Line 44**: `x_cluster = x[:, :, indices]` - Used boolean indexing which requires concrete values in JAX\n\nThese patterns work fine in eager mode but\
    \ fail when JAX tries to JIT-compile the training step.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Version 2**: Removed the problematic `if not jnp.any(indices):` check\n- Result: Eliminated TracerBoolConversionError\n- New error: NonConcreteBooleanIndexError on boolean indexing\n\n**Version 3**: Changed to integer indices using `jnp.where(...)[0]`\n- Result: Eliminated boolean indexing error\n- New error: ConcretizationTypeError - dynamic size for nonzero operation\n\n**Version 4** (SUCCESSFUL): Complete vectorization refactor\n- Replaced dynamic indexing with masked operations\n- Used `jnp.where(mask, value, 0.0)` for both input and output masking\n- Applied mask via broadcasting: `mask[None, None, :]` to match (B, T, N) shape\n- Accumulated results using addition instead of scatter operations\n- All operations are now JAX-JIT compatible\n\n## Key Changes in submission_v4.py\n\n```python\n# OLD (storage/episteme/smf_v1.py):\nfor i in range(self.num_clusters):\n    indices = jnp.where(self.cluster_assignments\
    \ == i, True, False)\n    if not jnp.any(indices):  # JAX tracer error\n        continue\n    x_cluster = x[:, :, indices]  # Dynamic indexing error\n    expert = SharedNeuronMLP(name=f\"expert_{i}\")\n    y_cluster = expert(x_cluster, training=training)\n    y_out = y_out.at[:, :, indices].set(y_cluster)\n\n# NEW (submission_v4.py):\nfor i in range(self.num_clusters):\n    mask = (self.cluster_assignments == i)\n    mask_expanded = mask[None, None, :]\n    x_masked = jnp.where(mask_expanded, x, 0.0)\n    expert = SharedNeuronMLP(name=f\"expert_{i}\")\n    y_cluster = expert(x_masked, training=training)\n    mask_output = mask[None, None, :]\n    y_masked = jnp.where(mask_output, y_cluster, 0.0)\n    y_out = y_out + y_masked\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix transforms gather-scatter operations into mask-and-accumulate operations:\n- **Gather**: Instead of indexing to extract cluster neurons, we mask the input (set non-cluster neurons to 0)\n- **Process**: Each expert processes\
    \ the full (B, T, N) tensor but only meaningful values are non-zero\n- **Scatter**: Instead of assigning to specific indices, we mask the output and accumulate all results\n- **Broadcasting**: `mask[None, None, :]` expands (N,) to (1, 1, N) for element-wise operations with (B, T, N)\n\nThis approach:\n- Works with JAX JIT compilation (no dynamic indexing)\n- Maintains the same logical behavior (each expert processes its cluster)\n- Uses slightly more computation (experts see zeros for non-cluster neurons) but gains JIT efficiency\n\n## Verification\n\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v4.py runs without crashing for over 300 seconds, indicating successful execution of the training validation step. The code is now JAX-JIT compatible and ready for full training.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\nimport numpy as np\nimport optax\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom smf_v1 import SharedNeuronMLP  # Keep import for working class\nfrom base_wrapper import BaseWrapper\n\n# --- Data Loading and Clustering ---\n# This happens once at the start of the script.\nNEURON_MEANS = np.load('storage/episteme/neuron_means.npy')\nNUM_CLUSTERS = 16\n\nprint(f\"Performing k-means clustering with k={NUM_CLUSTERS}...\")\nkmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=NUM_CLUSTERS, random_state=42, n_init='auto')\n# Reshape for sklearn: (n_samples, n_features)\ncluster_assignments_np = kmeans.fit_predict(NEURON_MEANS.reshape(-1, 1))\nCLUSTER_ASSIGNMENTS = jnp.array(cluster_assignments_np)\nprint(\"Clustering complete.\")\n\n# --- Fixed StaticModularForecaster ---\n# Completely refactored to be JAX-compatible with vectorized operations\nclass StaticModularForecaster(nn.Module):\n    num_clusters: int\n    cluster_assignments: jnp.ndarray\
    \ # Shape (N,)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        B, T, N = x.shape\n\n        # Create output tensor\n        y_out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        # Process each cluster separately (loop over num_clusters which is static)\n        for i in range(self.num_clusters):\n            # Create a mask for this cluster (boolean array)\n            mask = (self.cluster_assignments == i)  # Shape: (N,)\n\n            # Apply mask to select neurons - use broadcasting to handle batch and time dims\n            # mask shape: (N,) -> expand to (1, 1, N) for broadcasting\n            mask_expanded = mask[None, None, :]  # Shape: (1, 1, N)\n\n            # Apply mask: where mask is False, set to 0\n            x_masked = jnp.where(mask_expanded, x, 0.0)  # Shape: (B, T, N)\n\n            # Process through expert\n            expert = SharedNeuronMLP(name=f\"expert_{i}\")\n            y_cluster = expert(x_masked, training=training)  # Shape: (B,\
    \ 32, N)\n\n            # Only keep predictions where mask is True, using same broadcasting\n            mask_output = mask[None, None, :]  # Shape: (1, 1, N)\n            y_masked = jnp.where(mask_output, y_cluster, 0.0)  # Shape: (B, 32, N)\n\n            # Accumulate into output\n            y_out = y_out + y_masked\n\n        return y_out\n\n# --- Model Definition ---\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 1e-3,\n        'num_clusters': NUM_CLUSTERS,\n    }\n\nclass SMF_Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = StaticModularForecaster(\n            num_clusters=hparams['num_clusters'],\n            cluster_assignments=CLUSTER_ASSIGNMENTS\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False,\
    \ mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n            return output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SMF_Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\nPerforming k-means clustering with k=16...\nClustering complete.\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n\
    ✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\nPerforming k-means clustering with k=16...\nClustering complete.\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 45\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_clusters': 16}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.238443   |   0.047190  \n   2    |   0.034331   |   0.030022  \n   3    |   0.030404   |   0.030438  \n   4    |   0.030202   |   0.030205  \n   5    |   0.030126   |   0.030298  \n   6    |   0.030026   |   0.029729  \n   7    |   0.029872   |   0.029883  \n   8    |   0.029779   |   0.029538  \n   9    |   0.029697   |   0.029564  \n  10    |   0.029506   |   0.029530  \n  11    |   0.029484   | \
