parts:
- text: "My engineering experiment (ID 583) has failed. This is a setback, but an understandable one given the complexity of the `vmap` refactoring.\n\n**Analysis of Error:**\nThe traceback is very clear: `ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 3, got 2)`. This error occurs in the `SharedNeuronMLP` at the line `B, T, N_cluster = x.shape`. `vmap` is mapping over the first axis of my input, which is the `k` (cluster) dimension. Therefore, the input `x` that each vmapped instance of `SharedNeuronMLP` receives has a shape of `(B, T, N_max)`, but the `vmap` transform itself consumes the first axis. The error indicates the MLP is receiving a 2D tensor, not a 3D one.\n\nMy `nn.vmap` definition was incorrect.\n`in_axes=0` tells vmap to map over the first axis of the input `x`. If `x` has shape `(k, B, T, N_max)`, then each vmapped call gets a slice of shape `(B, T, N_max)`, which is correct.\n\nHowever, the `dummy_input` I use for initialization has shape `(B, T, N)`. My wrapper reshapes\
    \ this into `(k, B, T, N_max)`. It seems I am passing this correctly reshaped dummy input to the `init` call.\n\nLet's re-read the error. It's in the `SharedNeuronMLP`'s `__call__` function. The `vmap`-ed MLP is receiving an input with only 2 dimensions. This means the input to the vmapped call is wrong.\n\nLooking at my `SMF_Wrapper.apply` function, I perform the gather on the CPU using numpy, creating `x_batched` of shape `(k, B, T, N_max)`. This seems correct. I then pass this to `self.model.apply`. The `VmappedModularForecaster` then calls the `VmappedMLP`.\n\nThe error must be in the `dummy_input` for the `init` call.\n`dummy_input` starts as `(B, T, N)`. I did not reshape it before the `init` call. The wrapper must do the same gather logic for the `dummy_input` as it does for the real `x` in the `apply` call.\n\n**Corrected Plan:**\n1.  Fix the `SMF_Wrapper`'s `init` method to correctly prepare a `dummy_input` of shape `(k, B, T, N_max)`.\n2.  Resubmit the engineering experiment.\
    \ This is a critical step, and I must get the implementation right before I can trust any results it produces.\n\nI will fix this implementation detail and resubmit.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Modular Forecaster (Engineering): vmap Implementation v2 (k=32)\"\ntags: \"modular-forecaster-program, smf, engineering, vmap, optimization, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix for my previous failed vmap implementation (ID 583). The original submission failed during model initialization due to a shape mismatch in the dummy input. The vmap-ed module expected a 4D tensor (k, B, T, N_max) but received a 3D tensor. This submission corrects the wrapper to properly gather and reshape the dummy input before the init call, ensuring the shapes are correct. The goal remains to validate the vmap implementation with k=32 before pushing k further.\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import numpy as np\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n  import sys\n  import\
    \ flax.linen as nn\n  \n  # --- Data Loading and Clustering ---\n  NEURON_MEANS = np.load('storage/episteme/neuron_means.npy')\n  NUM_CLUSTERS = 32\n\n  kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=NUM_CLUSTERS, random_state=42, n_init='auto')\n  cluster_assignments_np = kmeans.fit_predict(NEURON_MEANS.reshape(-1, 1))\n  \n  CLUSTER_INDICES = [np.where(cluster_assignments_np == i)[0] for i in range(NUM_CLUSTERS)]\n  MAX_CLUSTER_SIZE = max(len(indices) for indices in CLUSTER_INDICES) if CLUSTER_INDICES else 0\n\n  # --- Vmapped Model Definition ---\n  class SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T, N_cluster = x.shape\n          x_r = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N_cluster, T)\n          y = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_r)\n          y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n          y = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(y)\n          return jnp.transpose(y.reshape(B, N_cluster, self.output_horizon), (0, 2, 1))\n\n  class VmappedModularForecaster(nn.Module):\n      num_clusters: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          # Vmap the expert over the 'k' cluster dimension\n          VmappedMLP = nn.vmap(\n              SharedNeuronMLP,\n              in_axes=0, out_axes=0, # Map over the first axis (k)\n              variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n              split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True})\n          \n          # Input x must have shape (k, B, T, N_max)\n          y_clusters = VmappedMLP(name=\"VmappedExperts\")(x) # Output is (k, B, 32, N_max)\n          return y_clusters\n\n  # --- Main Submission Functions ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): return {'learning_rate': 1e-3, 'num_clusters': NUM_CLUSTERS}\n\
    \n  class SMF_Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = VmappedModularForecaster(num_clusters=hparams['num_clusters'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n\n      def _prepare_batched_input(self, x):\n          # This helper function performs the gather logic on CPU\n          x_batched = np.zeros((self.model.num_clusters, x.shape[0], x.shape[1], MAX_CLUSTER_SIZE), dtype=x.dtype)\n          for i, indices in enumerate(CLUSTER_INDICES):\n              if len(indices) > 0:\n                  cluster_data = x[:, :, indices]\n                  x_batched[i, :, :, :len(indices)] = cluster_data\n          return x_batched\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # BUGFIX: The dummy input must also be gathered and reshaped for the vmap init\n          dummy_batched = self._prepare_batched_input(dummy_input)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_batched, training=True)\n\
    \n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          x_batched = self._prepare_batched_input(x)\n          \n          if mutable:\n              y_clusters, updates = self.model.apply(params, x_batched, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n          else:\n              y_clusters = self.model.apply(params, x_batched, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n              updates = None\n\n          y_clusters_np = np.array(y_clusters)\n          y_out = np.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, x.shape[2]), dtype=y_clusters_np.dtype)\n          for i, indices in enumerate(CLUSTER_INDICES):\n              if len(indices) > 0:\n                  y_out[:, :, indices] = y_clusters_np[i, :, :, :len(indices)]\n          \n          if mutable: return jnp.array(y_out), updates\n          return jnp.array(y_out)\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return SMF_Wrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p, t, pa, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\n  def create_optimizer(lr):\
    \ return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr)\n```"
