role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 326\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** The Modular Forecaster Program. Engineering Thrust: Re-implement SMF with `jax.vmap` to solve the computational bottleneck.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,493 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 112 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Modular Forecaster (Engineering): vmap Implementation v2 (k=32)' (ID: 586) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029149853993165536\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0237\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0271\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0305\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0323\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 586\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the JAX tracer error by converting NumPy operations to JAX operations in the data preparation methods.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code used NumPy operations (`np.zeros`, `np.array`, and NumPy array indexing) inside the `_prepare_batched_input` method of `SMF_Wrapper`. This method was called during the `apply` function, which was executed inside a JIT-compiled `train_step` function.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen JAX JIT-compiles a function, it traces through the computation graph.\
    \ During tracing, JAX arrays become \"tracers\" rather than concrete values. NumPy operations cannot work with JAX tracers, leading to:\n\n```\njax.errors.TracerArrayConversionError: The numpy.ndarray conversion method __array__()\nwas called on traced array with shape float32[4,4,6838]\n```\n\nThe error occurred specifically at line 65 in the original submission:\n```python\nx_batched[i, :, :, :len(indices)] = cluster_data  # NumPy indexing on JAX tracer!\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Changes in submission_v2.py:\n\n1. **Replaced NumPy with JAX in `_prepare_batched_input`:**\n   - Changed `np.zeros()` to `jnp.zeros()`\n   - Replaced NumPy indexing (`x_batched[i, :, :, :len(indices)] = cluster_data`) with JAX's immutable indexing pattern (`x_batched.at[i, :, :, :len(indices)].set(cluster_data)`)\n\n2. **Added new JAX-compatible scatter method:**\n   - Created `_scatter_batched_output` method to handle output scattering using JAX operations\n   - Replaced NumPy operations in the output\
    \ gathering logic with JAX equivalents\n\n3. **Updated `apply` method:**\n   - Modified to use the new `_scatter_batched_output` method instead of mixing NumPy/JAX operations\n   - Removed unnecessary NumPy conversions that broke JIT compilation\n\n### Key Technical Details:\n\n**Before (broken):**\n```python\nx_batched = np.zeros(...)  # NumPy array\nx_batched[i, :, :, :len(indices)] = cluster_data  # NumPy indexing\n```\n\n**After (fixed):**\n```python\nx_batched = jnp.zeros(...)  # JAX array\nx_batched = x_batched.at[i, :, :, :len(indices)].set(cluster_data)  # JAX indexing\n```\n\nJAX uses functional immutable arrays, so instead of in-place modification, we use the `.at[].set()` syntax which returns a new array with the updated values. This is compatible with JIT compilation and automatic differentiation.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix worked:\n- Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 (success)\n- The TracerArrayConversionError\
    \ is resolved\n\nThe evaluation may still be running to completion, but the critical issue (code crashing during training) has been fixed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpy as np\nimport optax\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# --- Data Loading and Clustering ---\nNEURON_MEANS = np.load('storage/episteme/neuron_means.npy')\nNUM_CLUSTERS = 32\n\nkmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=NUM_CLUSTERS, random_state=42, n_init='auto')\ncluster_assignments_np = kmeans.fit_predict(NEURON_MEANS.reshape(-1, 1))\n\nCLUSTER_INDICES = [np.where(cluster_assignments_np == i)[0] for i in range(NUM_CLUSTERS)]\nMAX_CLUSTER_SIZE = max(len(indices) for indices in CLUSTER_INDICES) if CLUSTER_INDICES else 0\n\n# --- Vmapped Model Definition ---\nclass SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T, N_cluster = x.shape\n        x_r = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N_cluster, T)\n        y = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_r)\n        y = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(y)\n        y = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(y)\n        return jnp.transpose(y.reshape(B, N_cluster, self.output_horizon), (0, 2, 1))\n\nclass VmappedModularForecaster(nn.Module):\n    num_clusters: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        # Vmap the expert over the 'k' cluster dimension\n        VmappedMLP = nn.vmap(\n            SharedNeuronMLP,\n            in_axes=0, out_axes=0, # Map over the first axis (k)\n            variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params':\
    \ True, 'dropout': True})\n\n        # Input x must have shape (k, B, T, N_max)\n        y_clusters = VmappedMLP(name=\"VmappedExperts\")(x) # Output is (k, B, 32, N_max)\n        return y_clusters\n\n# --- Main Submission Functions ---\nBASE_SEED = 42\ndef _define_hyperparameters(): return {'learning_rate': 1e-3, 'num_clusters': NUM_CLUSTERS}\n\nclass SMF_Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = VmappedModularForecaster(num_clusters=hparams['num_clusters'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n\n    def _prepare_batched_input(self, x):\n        # BUGFIX: Use JAX operations instead of NumPy to be JIT-compatible\n        # Pre-compute cluster data on CPU during init if possible, but for JIT,\n        # we need to use JAX operations\n        x_batched = jnp.zeros((self.model.num_clusters, x.shape[0], x.shape[1], MAX_CLUSTER_SIZE), dtype=x.dtype)\n        for i, indices in enumerate(CLUSTER_INDICES):\n            if len(indices)\
    \ > 0:\n                cluster_data = x[:, :, indices]\n                # Use JAX indexing instead of NumPy\n                x_batched = x_batched.at[i, :, :, :len(indices)].set(cluster_data)\n        return x_batched\n\n    def _scatter_batched_output(self, y_clusters, original_shape):\n        # BUGFIX: Use JAX operations for scatter as well\n        y_out = jnp.zeros((original_shape[0], 32, original_shape[2]), dtype=y_clusters.dtype)\n        for i, indices in enumerate(CLUSTER_INDICES):\n            if len(indices) > 0:\n                # Use JAX indexing\n                y_out = y_out.at[:, :, indices].set(y_clusters[i, :, :, :len(indices)])\n        return y_out\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # The dummy input must also be gathered and reshaped for the vmap init\n        dummy_batched = self._prepare_batched_input(dummy_input)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_batched, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params,\
    \ x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        x_batched = self._prepare_batched_input(x)\n\n        if mutable:\n            y_clusters, updates = self.model.apply(params, x_batched, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n        else:\n            y_clusters = self.model.apply(params, x_batched, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n            updates = None\n\n        y_out = self._scatter_batched_output(y_clusters, x.shape)\n\n        if mutable: return y_out, updates\n        return y_out\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return SMF_Wrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(p, t, pa, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\ndef create_optimizer(lr): return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\n\
    Parallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 45\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_clusters': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031708   |   0.029499  \n   2    |   0.028992   |   0.029386  \n   3    |   0.028932   |   0.029421  \n   4    |   0.028912   |   0.029312  \n   5    |   0.028888   |   0.029276  \n   6    |   0.028881   |   0.029313  \n   7    |   0.028880   |   0.029335  \n   8    |   0.028872   |   0.029289  \n   9    |   0.028858   |\
    \   0.029290  \n  10    |   0.028848   |   0.029253  \n  11    |   0.028839   |   0.029295  \n  12    |   0.028849   |   0.029222  \n  13    |   0.028832   |   0.029297  \n  14    |   0.028832   |   0.029298  \n  15    |   0.028833   |   0.029232  \n  16    |   0.028838   |   0.029197  \n  17    |   0.028819   |   0.029186  \n  18    |   0.028817   |   0.029263  \n  19    |   0.028810   |   0.029350  \n  20    |   0.028822   |   0.029270  \n  21    |   0.028816   |   0.029280  \n  22    |   0.028807   |   0.029307  \n  23    |   0.028812   |   0.029150  \n  24    |   0.028805   |   0.029205  \n  25    |   0.028811   |   0.029322  \n  26    |   0.028807   |   0.029239  \n  27    |   0.028806   |   0.029266  \n  28    |   0.028812   |   0.029205  \n  29    |   0.028800   |   0.029207  \n  30    |   0.028797   |   0.029180  \n  31    |   0.028789   |   0.029196  \n  32    |   0.028797   |   0.029259  \n  33    |   0.028791   |   0.029223  \n  34    |   0.028793   |   0.029172  \n  35  \
