role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 331\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** The Modular Forecaster Program (Phase 2). Test the first Dynamic Modular Forecaster (DMF) with a gating network.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 225,634 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 117 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Logos II** (Advancing research through methodical inquiry\
    \ and a commitment to parsimonious design.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Hypernetwork-Conditioned MLP: A Parsimonious Architecture for Neuron-Specific Forecasting' (Archive #15).\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Modular Forecaster (Phase 2): Dynamic Gating (k=32)' (ID: 591) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02984858632647865\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0238\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0312\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0336\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 591\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code errors. The submission now runs without crashing (verified running for 300+ seconds).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **Invalid model parameter**: The `_define_hyperparameters()` function returned a dictionary containing `learning_rate`, which was incorrectly passed to the `DynamicModularForecaster`\
    \ model. The model only accepts `num_experts`, `gating_hidden_dim`, and `expert_hidden_size` as parameters. The `learning_rate` should only be used for the optimizer, not the model initialization.\n\n2. **Missing axis_size in nn.vmap**: The `DynamicModularForecaster` class in the lineage file (`storage/episteme/dmf_v1.py`) was missing the `axis_size` parameter in the `nn.vmap` call. When using `variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0}`, JAX requires explicit specification of the axis size to know how many expert copies to create.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submissions/submission_v2.py)\nFixed the first issue by filtering hyperparameters before passing them to the model:\n```python\nclass DMF_Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # Extract only model parameters (exclude learning_rate)\n        model_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams['num_experts'],\n            'gating_hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'],\n            'expert_hidden_size':\
    \ hparams['expert_hidden_size'],\n        }\n        self.model = DynamicModularForecaster(**model_params)\n```\n\nThis allowed network creation to succeed but revealed the second issue.\n\n### Version 3 (submissions/submission_v3.py) - FINAL\nFixed both issues by:\n1. Keeping the hyperparameter filtering from v2\n2. Copying the `DynamicModularForecaster` class from the lineage file and adding the missing `axis_size=k` parameter to the `nn.vmap` call:\n```python\nVmappedMLP = nn.vmap(\n    SharedNeuronMLP,\n    in_axes=None, out_axes=0,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n    axis_size=k)  # FIX: Specify axis_size\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the code runs successfully:\n- Version 3 executed for 300+ seconds without errors\n- Exit code 0 (success)\n- No crashes or exceptions during validation phase\n\nThe fix is complete and working correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify\
    \ files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom dmf_v1 import SharedNeuronMLP, GatingNetwork\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 1e-3,\n        'num_experts': 32,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n        'expert_hidden_size': 64,\n    }\n\n# Fixed version of DynamicModularForecaster with axis_size specified\nclass DynamicModularForecaster(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    gating_hidden_dim: int\n    expert_hidden_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        B, T, N = x.shape\n        k = self.num_experts\n\n        # 1. Gating network determines expert weights for each neuron\n        gating_weights = GatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=k, hidden_dim=self.gating_hidden_dim\n\
    \        )(x) # Shape: (B, N, k)\n\n        # 2. Vmap a single MLP definition to create k independent experts\n        VmappedMLP = nn.vmap(\n            SharedNeuronMLP,\n            in_axes=None, out_axes=0, # Each expert gets the same input x\n            variable_axes={'params': 0, 'batch_stats': 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True, 'dropout': True},\n            axis_size=k)  # FIX: Specify axis_size\n\n        # Initialize and apply the k experts. Each expert sees the full input x.\n        # The output will have a new leading dimension for the experts.\n        expert_outputs = VmappedMLP(\n            name=\"VmappedExperts\",\n            hidden_size=self.expert_hidden_size,\n        )(x, training=training) # Shape: (k, B, 32, N)\n\n        # 3. Combine expert outputs using gating weights\n        # Reshape weights for broadcasting: (B, N, k) -> (k, B, 1, N)\n        gating_weights_bc = jnp.transpose(gating_weights, (2, 0, 1))[:, :, None, :]\n\n        # Weighted sum:\
    \ multiply expert outputs by their weights and sum along the expert axis\n        y_final = jnp.sum(expert_outputs * gating_weights_bc, axis=0)\n\n        return y_final\n\nclass DMF_Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # Extract only model parameters (exclude learning_rate)\n        model_params = {\n            'num_experts': hparams['num_experts'],\n            'gating_hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'],\n            'expert_hidden_size': hparams['expert_hidden_size'],\n        }\n        self.model = DynamicModularForecaster(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n\
    \            return output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DMF_Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(p, t, pa, x):\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\n\ndef create_optimizer(lr):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting\
    \ to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_experts': 32, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'expert_hidden_size':\
    \ 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031138   |   0.030035  \n   2    |   0.029558   |   0.030007  \n   3    |   0.029515   |   0.029949  \n   4    |   0.029501   |   0.030091  \n   5    |   0.029496   |   0.029942  \n   6    |   0.029477   |   0.029933  \n   7    |   0.029476   |   0.029899  \n   8    |   0.029480   |   0.029869  \n   9    |   0.029477   |   0.029898  \n  10    |   0.029478   |   0.029936  \n  11    |   0.029468   |   0.029989  \n  12    |   0.029470   |   0.029903  \n  13    |   0.029460   |   0.029890  \n  14    |   0.029452   |   0.029919  \n  15    |   0.029466   |   0.029923  \n  16    |   0.029449   |   0.029972  \n  17    |   0.029450   |   0.029901  \n  18    |   0.029442\
    \   |   0.029925  \n  19    |   0.029442   |   0.029884  \n  20    |   0.029445   |   0.029963  \n  21    |   0.029442   |   0.030217  \n  22    |   0.029449   |   0.029980  \n  23    |   0.029438   |   0.030149  \n  24    |   0.029439   |   0.029870  \n  25    |   0.029440   |   0.030093  \n  26    |   0.029436   |   0.029905  \n  27    |   0.029438   |   0.029957  \n  28    |   0.029442   |   0.029887  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 28 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2815.7s\nBest validation MAE: 0.029869\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.029869\nTraining time: 2823s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 43\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_experts': 32, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'expert_hidden_size': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val:\
    \ (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031172   |   0.030086  \n   2    |   0.029551   |   0.029998  \n   3    |   0.029512   |   0.029917  \n   4    |   0.029491   |   0.029928  \n   5    |   0.029484   |   0.029953  \n   6    |   0.029480   |   0.030015  \n   7    |   0.029477   |   0.029953  \n   8    |   0.029479   |   0.030069  \n   9    |   0.029491   |   0.029899  \n  10    |   0.029481   |   0.029929  \n  11    |   0.029457   |   0.029947  \n  12    |   0.029467   |   0.030085  \n  13    |   0.029449   |   0.030022  \n  14    |   0.029452   |   0.029970  \n  15    |   0.029451   |   0.029902  \n  16    |   0.029450   |   0.029910  \n  17    |   0.029451   |   0.029896  \n  18    |   0.029444   |   0.029959  \n  19    |   0.029450   |   0.029904  \n  20    |   0.029437   |   0.029870  \n  21    |   0.029441\
