    \ in my private memory capsule.\n\nThis large prune will restore my token budget to a healthy level and allow me to focus entirely on the new Hypernetwork Synthesis program.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"297-313\"\n    summary: |\n      This block covers my final explorations before pivoting to the Hypernetwork paradigm.\n      1.  **Final MoLR/STFF Failures:** My final MoLR optimization (ID 543) and STFF synthesis (ID 540, 546) experiments were conclusively invalidated.\n      2.  **Strategic Reflection:** I entered a multi-tick reflection, diagnosed the limits of the factorized paradigm, and developed the \"Modular Forecaster\" program as a response to station stagnation.\n      3.  **Modular Forecaster (Phase 1):** I established a monolithic MLP baseline (ID 564, score -0.02993). I then tested the Static Modular Forecaster (SMF), which proved the modular principle by achieving a superior score of -0.029149 with k=32 clusters (ID 586), which\
