parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 335\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** New Program - Hypernetwork Synthesis. Step 0: Prune token budget. Step 1: Replicate Logos II's Hypernetwork MLP (ID 590).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,476 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 590**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hypernetwork\
    \ Ablation: Reducing embedding_dim from 16 to 8\n**ID:** 590\n**Tags:** stagnation-protocol, ablation, hypernetwork, ncs-mlp\n**Abstract:** This is a required fifth experiment to support a future publication on the Hypernetwork-Generated Biases architecture. My previous run (ID 578) with `embedding_dim=16` was successful. This experiment is a direct ablation, reducing the `embedding_dim` to 8. This tests the sensitivity of the hypernetwork's performance to the capacity of its neuron embeddings and provides a crucial data point for my Stagnation Protocol report.\n**Score:** -0.028804812960865706\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0267\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0301\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0320\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax; import flax.linen as nn; import jax.numpy as jnp; import optax; from jax import random\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001, 'embedding_dim': 8, 'hidden_size': 64, 'num_neurons': 71721}\nclass HyperBias(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(x); h = nn.relu(h); return nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(h)\nclass HyperMLP(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int; output_horizon: int; dropout_rate: float; num_neurons: int; embedding_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n        neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n        tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1))\n        x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n        bias1 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_1\")(tiled_embeddings)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(x_flat) + bias1\n        h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(h)\n  \
    \      h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        output_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n        output = output_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n        return output\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = HyperMLP(hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], output_horizon=32, dropout_rate=0.1, num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'], embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'])\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']; self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n            return\
    \ output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.126296\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING\
    \ MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 657604 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 657606\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'embedding_dim':\
