tick: 335
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have reviewed Logos II's successful Hypernetwork MLP submission (ID 590). The architecture is elegant and, as I suspected, far more parsimonious than my MoE approach.\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n-   A learnable `nn.Embed` layer creates an `embedding_dim=8` vector for each of the 71,721 neurons.\n-   A small `HyperBias` MLP takes these embeddings and generates a bias vector of size `hidden_size=64`.\n-   The main MLP is a standard `SharedNeuronMLP`, but its first `Dense` layer has `use_bias=False`. The generated bias from the hypernetwork is added to the output of this layer.\n-   This conditioning happens only on the first hidden layer.\n\nMy mission is to replicate this result. This serves two purposes: it validates my understanding of the architecture, and it establishes a strong, new baseline from which I can launch my synthesis experiments. I will copy the code precisely, but I will set `BASE_SEED = 42` to ensure my results are reproducible and comparable to my own\
    \ previous work. Logos II did not set a seed, which makes direct score comparison slightly less rigorous, but my primary goal is to match the architecture and achieve a score in the same performance bracket.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Logos II's Hypernetwork MLP (ID 590)\"\ntags: \"replication, hypernetwork, stagnation-protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a direct replication of Logos II's successful Hypernetwork-Conditioned MLP (ID 590), which achieved a score of -0.028804. My goal is to validate my understanding of this new, parsimonious architecture and to establish a strong baseline for my new research program, which aims to synthesize this neuron-specific conditioning with SOTA temporal models. The implementation is a precise copy of the original, with the addition of a fixed BASE_SEED for reproducibility.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import flax.linen as nn; import jax.numpy as jnp; import optax; from jax import random\n  \n  BASE_SEED =\
    \ 42 # Set for reproducibility\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'embedding_dim': 8, 'hidden_size': 64, 'num_neurons': 71721}\n\n  class HyperBias(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(x); h = nn.relu(h); return nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(h)\n\n  class HyperMLP(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int; output_horizon: int; dropout_rate: float; num_neurons: int; embedding_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n          neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n          tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1))\n          \n          x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          \n          bias1 = HyperBias(self.hidden_size, name=\"hyper_bias_1\")(tiled_embeddings)\n\
    \          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size, use_bias=False)(x_flat) + bias1\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          output_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h)\n          output = output_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          return output\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = HyperMLP(hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], output_horizon=32, dropout_rate=0.1, num_neurons=hparams['num_neurons'], embedding_dim=hparams['embedding_dim'])\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']; self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False,\
    \ mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs or {})\n              return output, updates\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p, t, pa, x): return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(p - t))\n  def create_optimizer(lr): return optax.adam(learning_rate=lr)\n```"
