tick: 337
role: model
parts:
- text: "My replication experiment (ID 599) has succeeded.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\n-   **My Replication Score:** -0.028841\n-   **Logos II's Original Score:** -0.028804 (ID 590)\n\nThe scores are extremely close. The minor difference can be attributed to the stochasticity of training, especially since the original submission did not use a fixed `BASE_SEED`. I have successfully replicated the architecture and performance of the Hypernetwork-Conditioned MLP.\n\n**Consolidation:**\nStep 1 of my new research program is complete. I now have a validated, high-performing, non-factorized baseline. This model is the current \"local SOTA\" for simple architectures that have abandoned the factorized paradigm, and it significantly outperforms my previous best non-factorized model.\n\n**Path Forward: The Synthesis**\nNow, I can proceed to the core hypothesis of my new research program: **Synthesizing the neuron-specific conditioning of the Hypernetwork MLP with the superior temporal modeling of\
    \ the factorized SOTA.**\n\n**Hypothesis:** I will create a hybrid model. It will retain the factorized structure of the SOTA (Fourier branch + Residual branch), but I will replace the simple `SharedNeuronMLP` inside the factor projection/expansion layers with the more powerful Hypernetwork MLP. This will allow the model to learn neuron-specific factor loadings, a concept that has not yet been explored. This synthesis should outperform both the pure Hypernetwork MLP (-0.0288) and the pure factorized SOTA (-0.0261).\n\n**Experiment Plan:**\n1.  **Architecture:** I will need to carefully integrate the `HyperMLP` into the factorized backbone. I will take the SOTA architecture code (from my successful replication in ID 519) and replace the `nn.Dense` layers in the factor expansion with the `HyperMLP` structure. This is a complex integration.\n2.  **Control:** The baseline for this experiment is the pure SOTA factorized model.\n3.  **Goal:** Achieve a score better than -0.026125.\n\nThis\
    \ is the most ambitious experiment I have designed. I will first document the successful replication and then begin the complex task of writing the synthesis code.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 20}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Addendum: Hypernetwork Replication Success & Initiation of Synthesis Program**\n\n  My replication of Logos II's Hypernetwork MLP (ID 599) was a success. My score of -0.028841 is statistically identical to the original (-0.028804). I now have a validated, high-performance, non-factorized baseline.\n\n  **Initiating Phase 2: Hypernetwork-Factorized Synthesis**\n  I will now proceed with the core hypothesis of my new program. I will attempt to synthesize the neuron-specific conditioning of the Hypernetwork MLP with the powerful temporal modeling of the SOTA factorized architecture. My hypothesis is that using the Hypernetwork to learn neuron-specific factor projections will outperform both parent architectures.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **My Protocol:**\n  1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n  2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n  3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n  4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n  **Current Mission:** New Program - Hypernetwork Synthesis. Step 2: Integrate Hypernetwork MLP into the SOTA factorized backbone.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
