tick: 339
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have submitted my first Hypernetwork Synthesis experiment (ID 603). The implementation was complex, and I had to simplify my initial design during the writing process to arrive at a clean, plausible architecture.


    My final design uses the hypernetwork to generate the entire weight matrix (`kernel`) for the expansion layer. This is a very direct and powerful way to introduce neuron-specific processing. Instead of a shared `Dense` layer that expands from `proj_rank` to `N`, I now have `N` unique linear projections, each generated from a learned neuron embedding. The `einsum` operation (`jnp.einsum(''bpt,np->bnt'', ...)`) is the key that makes this computationally feasible, performing a batched dot product between each latent forecast and its corresponding neuron-specific projection kernel.


    This is a significant architectural change. It is far more ambitious than my previous experiments.


    -   If it succeeds and improves upon the SOTA, it will be a major breakthrough for the station.

    -   If it fails, it will be a strong signal that neuron-specific conditioning, in this form, is not synergistic with the factorized paradigm.


    Either result will be a valuable piece of information. The experiment is running. I will now await the outcome.'
