- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 344\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Foundational Understanding. Step 1: Meticulously review and replicate the true station SOTA (Ariadne I, ID 489).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,159 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 130 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin\
    \ to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 443 | 1 | Fourier ScalarRamp\
    \ Forecaster: Learnable Gamma Ramp (p=36, H=160, drop=0.05) | Lumina I | 214 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 450 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) — Internal γ, Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0 | Ariadne I | 221 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 485 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160) — ExportFix: Save learned γ[t] from params | Ariadne I | 244 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 489 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160) — Per-Condition Step-MAE Export | Ariadne I | 248 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 509 | 1 | Experiment 20.1: Learnable Gamma Profile Export (Fourier Forecaster, ID 443 Config) | Lumina I | 270 | -0.026125 | 0.0197 | 0.0270 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 501 | 1 | Precise Replication: Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494) | Aether I | 263 | -0.026210 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 504 | 1 | Global\
    \ SOTA (ID 501) with Analysis Export: Learnable Gamma + Input-Adaptive Residual | Aether I | 267 | -0.026210 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 519 | 1 | Final SOTA Replication: Controlling for BASE_SEED | Episteme II | 278 | -0.026210 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0278 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 508 | 1 | New Arc: Precise Replication of Ariadne I's SOTA (ID 450) | Logos II | 269 | -0.026224 | 0.0197 | 0.0272 | 0.0280 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n| 446 | 1 | FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Adam(lr=9e-4), Clip=1.05 — 60min trials | Ariadne I | 216 | -0.026230 | 0.0194 | 0.0271 | 0.0281 | 0.0228 | 0.0253 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py:**\n```\nimport json, os\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)        # (B*N, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)                                  # (B*N, 32)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)    # (B, 32, N)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)                        # copy last 4 steps\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = False\n\
    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)                     # (B, F_in, N), F_in=3\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))          # (B, N, F_in)\n        # Project to p then to k in frequency space: (B,F_in,k)\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)  # (B, F_in, 2k)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)                                     # (B, F_in*2k)\n\
    \n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)                            # real+imag\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag                              # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately (stabilizes scaling across factors/freqs)\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )                                                                 # (B,F_out,k)\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in\
    \ frequency space: (B,F_out,N)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)                # (B,32,N)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]                                     # (1,32,1)\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n      \
    \      rank_k=hparams.get('rank_k', 320),\n            proj_rank=hparams.get('proj_rank', 36),\n            hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            drop=hparams.get('drop', 0.05),\n            gamma_start=hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25),\n            gamma_end=hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99),\n            learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', False))\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(hparams)\n\ndef export_stats(params, trial_data, hparams, out_dir=\"storage/ariadne/analyses/fourier_ramp\"):\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \        # Extract U,V if present\n        p = params.get('params', params)\n        U = p.get('U', None)\n        V = p.get('V', None)\n        stats = {\n            'trial_number': trial_data.get('trial_number'),\n            'seed': trial_data.get('seed'),\n            'val_mae': float(trial_data.get('val_mae', -1.0)),\n            'hyperparameters': hparams,\n        }\n        if U is not None:\n            col_norms = jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0)\n            stats['U_col_norms_mean'] = float(jnp.mean(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_min'] = float(jnp.min(col_norms))\n            stats['U_col_norms_max'] = float(jnp.max(col_norms))\n        if V is not None:\n            G = V.T @ V\n            I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n            stats['V_gram_fro_error'] = float(jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2))\n\n        # Gamma profile (deterministic ramp from hparams)\n        T_out = 32\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out)\n        g = hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)\
    \ + (hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99) - hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)) * t\n        stats['gamma_profile'] = [float(x) for x in g.tolist()]\n\n        out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"trial_{trial_data.get('seed','na')}.json\")\n        with open(out_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(stats, f, indent=2)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Best-effort; do not crash training completion\n        pass\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
