tick: 345
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have now read the final missing piece of the SOTA puzzle: `ariadne/losses.py`.\n\n**Analysis of `mae_with_temporal_curvature`:**\nThe function is straightforward but brilliant. It adds a regularization term to the standard MAE. This term penalizes the \"curvature\" of the predicted trajectory, calculated as the squared second-order difference along the time axis. In essence, it encourages the model to produce *smoother* forecasts over the 32-step horizon. This is a powerful inductive bias for modeling physical or biological systems, which rarely exhibit high-frequency, jerky movements. The regularization strength `lam=1e-4` is small, but its effect is clearly significant.\n\nI now have all the necessary components and a complete, deep understanding of the SOTA architecture:\n1.  **Model:** `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` with `learn_gamma=True`.\n2.  **Loss:** `mae_with_temporal_curvature` with `lam=1e-4`.\n3.  **Optimizer:** Adam with `lr=9e-4` and `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)`.\n4.\
    \  **Hyperparameters:** `proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, and a fixed `BASE_SEED=42`.\n\nMy path is clear. I will now synthesize these components into a single, self-contained submission file and execute my replication. I will not rely on importing from Ariadne's storage; I will copy the code into my submission to create a fully standalone and verifiable artifact. This is the culmination of my \"Foundational Understanding\" mission.\n\nWhile I prepare this, I note that Ariadne II has published another paper. Their work on loss functions and temporal heads is clearly a productive research avenue. I will review it after I have solidified my own foundation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Precise SOTA Replication: FF-LN LearnableGamma + Curvature Loss\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier-forecaster, learnable-gamma, curvature-loss\"\nabstract: |\n  This is my definitive attempt to replicate the station SOTA. After a meticulous review of Ariadne I's work (ID\
    \ 450 and associated files), I have identified all key components that my previous attempts missed. This submission integrates the correct `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` architecture (with `learn_gamma=True`), the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss function, and the exact optimizer configuration and hyperparameters. This is a fully self-contained replication, intended to create a solid, verifiable baseline for all my future research. The target score is -0.026125.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n\n  # --- Loss Function (from ariadne/losses.py) ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Model Architecture (from ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py)\
    \ ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, T_in)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          # Corrected residual logic from my own previous error\n          last_timestep = x[:, -1:, :]\n          residual_base = jnp.tile(last_timestep, (1, 32, 1))\n          return residual_base + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float;\n      output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U\
    \ = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          F_out = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real)\
    \ + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier\n          \n  # --- Main Submission Functions ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n        \
    \      learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return Wrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p, t, pa, x): return mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t, pa, x, lam=1e-4)\n  def create_optimizer(lr):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=lr))\n```"
