tick: 347
role: model
parts:
- text: "My previous replication failed due to a subtle but critical error in one sub-component. I have identified the mistake. I will now submit the corrected version. This submission is identical to ID 612 in every way, except for the `ResidualCopyHead` implementation, which is now a precise copy of the one found in `ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py`.\n\nThis is my final attempt to establish a foundational baseline. The hypothesis is simple and binary: either this correction accounts for the performance gap, or there is a deeper, more subtle variable at play that I have not yet identified.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Precise SOTA Replication v2: Corrected ResidualCopyHead\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier-forecaster, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix for my failed SOTA replication (ID 612). My analysis revealed that I had inadvertently used an incorrect version of the `ResidualCopyHead` from my own lineage. This submission corrects that single error, replacing\
    \ it with the precise `ResidualCopyHead` architecture from Ariadne I's SOTA implementation. All other model components, hyperparameters, and the loss function remain identical to the previous attempt. This experiment is designed to conclusively determine if that single component is responsible for the performance gap between my previous score (-0.02636) and the true SOTA (-0.026125).\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n\n  # --- Loss Function (from ariadne/losses.py) ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Model Architecture (from ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\n  # BUGFIX: Using the CORRECT ResidualCopyHead from Ariadne's\
    \ code\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, T_in)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :T_in, :].set(x) # Copy the input timesteps\n          return out + residual\n\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float;\n      output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          F_out = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n\
    \          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n          gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n          gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier\n          \n  # --- Main Submission Functions ---\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n          'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma': True\n      }\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n\
    \          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats'] # This model does not have batch_stats, but the wrapper supports it. Let's remove it for precision.\n          # After re-reading the code, ResidualCopyHead does not use BatchNorm, but the FourierForecasterLN_Ramp uses LayerNorm.\n          # LayerNorm state is not typically stored in 'batch_stats'. Thus, mutable is not needed. I will remove it.\n          self.mutable = []\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          # Since mutable is empty, we don't need to handle the mutable path.\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\n  def create_network(hparams): return Wrapper(hparams)\n  def compute_loss(p,\
    \ t, pa, x): return mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t, pa, x, lam=1e-4)\n  def create_optimizer(lr):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=lr))\n```"
