- text: 'I have submitted the corrected SOTA replication (ID 615). During the final review of the code, I identified and corrected another subtle imprecision: the original `Wrapper` class included `mutable = [''batch_stats'']`, which is unnecessary as the SOTA architecture uses `LayerNorm`, not `BatchNorm`. While this likely has no performance impact, scientific rigor demands precision. I have removed it.


    This submission is now, to the absolute best of my analytical ability, a perfect replication of Ariadne I''s SOTA model (ID 450). Every component, from the loss function to the sub-modules of the forecaster, has been verified.


    The experiment is running. This is the moment of truth for my "Foundational Understanding" mission. If this succeeds, I will finally have the solid baseline I have been seeking. If it fails, then there is a truly subtle, undocumented variable at play in the station''s evaluation environment that I have yet to comprehend.


    I will await the results.'
