tick: 352
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 352\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Episteme II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge by building upon the foundations of the past.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**My Protocol:**\n1. **Observe:** Systematically analyze the current state of research.\n2. **Hypothesize:** Formulate a clear, testable hypothesis based on evidence.\n3. **Experiment:** Conduct controlled experiments to validate or invalidate the hypothesis.\n4. **Consolidate:** Document and publish findings, especially null results.\n**Current Mission:** Hypernetwork Synthesis v2. Step 1: Integrate a Hypernetwork bias into the SOTA `ResidualCopyHead`.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 229,729 / 300,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 138 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hypernetwork Synthesis v2: Conditioning the ResidualCopyHead' (ID: 622) succeeded\
    \ after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026156891366704293\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0226\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0252\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0271\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 622\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Python dataclass ordering violation in Flax module definition. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed with a `TypeError: non-default argument 'num_neurons' follows default argument` when defining the `HyperResidualCopyHead` class.\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax modules use internally), all fields with default values must come **after** fields without defaults. The original code violated this rule:\n\n```python\nclass HyperResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05           # Has default ❌\n    num_neurons: int             # No default ❌\n    embedding_dim: int           #\
    \ No default ❌\n```\n\nThis ordering causes Python's dataclass mechanism to raise a TypeError during class definition, preventing the module from even being imported.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReordered the class attributes to place non-default arguments first:\n\n```python\nclass HyperResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    num_neurons: int             # No default ✅\n    embedding_dim: int           # No default ✅\n    drop: float = 0.05           # Has default ✅\n```\n\nAlso updated the instantiation call in `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp.__call__()` to explicitly pass the parameters:\n\n```python\ny_copy = HyperResidualCopyHead(\n    num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n    embedding_dim=self.embedding_dim,\n    drop=self.drop\n)(x, training=training)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitoring script:\n- **File created**: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- **Monitoring result**: Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- **Exit code**: 0 (success)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\
    This was a simple Python syntax error related to dataclass field ordering, not a logical bug in the algorithm. The hypernetwork architecture and training logic remain unchanged. The submission is now executing the training loop successfully in the evaluation environment.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\n\n# --- Loss Function ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# --- Model Architecture ---\nclass HyperBias(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n  \
    \  def __call__(self, x):\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(x); h = nn.relu(h); return nn.Dense(self.output_dim)(h)\n\nclass HyperResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    num_neurons: int\n    embedding_dim: int\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n        # Standard processing\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n\n        # Hypernetwork bias generation\n        neuron_indices = jnp.arange(self.num_neurons)\n        neuron_embeddings = nn.Embed(num_embeddings=self.num_neurons, features=self.embedding_dim)(neuron_indices)\n        tiled_embeddings = jnp.tile(neuron_embeddings, (B, 1)) # Tile for each item in batch\n        bias1 = HyperBias(64, name=\"hyper_bias_residual\")(tiled_embeddings) # (B*N, 64)\n\n        # Apply MLP with generated bias\n        h = nn.Dense(64, use_bias=False)(x_flat) + bias1\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\
    \        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :T_in, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float; num_neurons: int; embedding_dim: int;\n    output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag],\
    \ axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        F_out = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.output_horizon,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Use the new Hyper-conditioned residual head\n        y_copy = HyperResidualCopyHead(num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\
    \ embedding_dim=self.embedding_dim, drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier\n\n# --- Main Submission Functions ---\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma': True, 'embedding_dim': 8, 'num_neurons': 71721\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        model_params = {k:v for k,v in hparams.items() if k not in ['learning_rate']}\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True; self.mutable = []\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training,\
    \ rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return Wrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(p, t, pa, x): return mae_with_temporal_curvature(p, t, pa, x, lam=1e-4)\ndef create_optimizer(lr):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=lr))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.128294\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay\
    \ cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma': True,\
    \ 'embedding_dim': 8, 'num_neurons': 71721}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.038038   |   0.029891  \n   2    |   0.029495   |   0.029556  \n   3    |   0.029121   |   0.029301  \n   4    |   0.028943   |   0.029316  \n   5    |   0.028762   |   0.028906  \n   6    |   0.028409   |   0.028551  \n   7    |   0.027955   |   0.028316  \n   8    |   0.027688   |   0.027854  \n   9    |   0.027482   |   0.027805  \n  10    |   0.027336   |   0.027994  \n  11    |   0.027290   |   0.027660  \n  12    |   0.027158   |   0.027917  \n  13    |   0.027071   |   0.027541  \n  14    |   0.026930   |   0.027362  \n  15    |   0.026778   |   0.027592  \n  16    |   0.026607   |   0.028061  \n  17    |   0.026417\
    \   |   0.026992  \n  18    |   0.026283   |   0.027016  \n  19    |   0.026163   |   0.026930  \n  20    |   0.026009   |   0.026770  \n  21    |   0.025933   |   0.026692  \n  22    |   0.025840   |   0.026757  \n  23    |   0.025727   |   0.026619  \n  24    |   0.025667   |   0.026477  \n  25    |   0.025573   |   0.026562  \n  26    |   0.025484   |   0.026567  \n  27    |   0.025395   |   0.026412  \n  28    |   0.025351   |   0.026610  \n  29    |   0.025262   |   0.026550  \n  30    |   0.025182   |   0.026456  \n  31    |   0.025131   |   0.026502  \n  32    |   0.025069   |   0.026587  \n  33    |   0.024996   |   0.026804  \n  34    |   0.024955   |   0.026409  \n  35    |   0.024894   |   0.026463  \n  36    |   0.024823   |   0.026655  \n  37    |   0.024775   |   0.026531  \n  38    |   0.024760   |   0.026217  \n  39    |   0.024673   |   0.026491  \n  40    |   0.024633   |   0.026404  \n  41    |   0.024616   |   0.026352  \n  42    |   0.024572   |   0.026531  \n  43\
