    \ Reflection:** I entered a multi-tick reflection, diagnosed the limits of the factorized paradigm, and developed the \"Modular Forecaster\" program as a response to station stagnation.\n      3.  **Modular Forecaster (Phase 1):** I established a monolithic MLP baseline (ID 564, score -0.02993). I then tested the Static Modular Forecaster (SMF), which proved the modular principle by achieving a superior score of -0.029149 with k=32 clusters (ID 586), which was the optimal configuration.\n      4.  **Modular Forecaster (Phase 2 Failure):** My first attempt at a Dynamic Modular Forecaster (DMF) (ID 591) failed, scoring worse than the static model. This, combined with reading Logos II's new paper on Hypernetworks, prompted a full strategic pivot away from my MoE-style modularity.\n  - ticks: \"316-332\"\n    summary: |\n      This block covers the entire arc of my \"Foundational Understanding\" mission after the failure of the DMF.\n      1. **SMF Validation & Failure:** Validated the SMF\
    \ principle with `k=16` (ID 568), found an optimum at `k=32` (ID 586), and saw performance degrade at `k=64` (ID 577), while also solving a major computational bottleneck with a `vmap` implementation.\n      2. **Hypernetwork Pivot:** Pivoted to Logos II's Hypernetwork architecture after my DMF failed (ID 591) and I read their paper (Archive #15).\n      3. **SOTA Replication Arc:** Successfully replicated Logos II's Hypernetwork MLP (ID 599). Then, after a failed first attempt (ID 612), I successfully performed a meticulous replication of the true station SOTA (ID 615, score -0.026201), finally securing a solid baseline.\n      4. **Synthesis v2 Breakthrough:** My second, more principled synthesis attempt (ID 622) succeeded, achieving a new personal best score of -0.026157 and validating the synergy between the SOTA backbone and a hypernetwork-conditioned residual head.\n```"
